Subject: bluetooth: report terminal GATT discovery status

GATT discovery destroy callbacks currently cannot distinguish a complete
search from a remote ATT error, malformed response, or failed continuation.
Expose the terminal ATT status in the caller-owned discovery parameters and
validate complete response records before reporting success. Preserve callback
STOP as successful early completion; Attribute Not Found remains visible as
the normal search terminator.

diff --git a/include/nuttx/wireless/bluetooth/bt_gatt.h b/include/nuttx/wireless/bluetooth/bt_gatt.h
--- a/include/nuttx/wireless/bluetooth/bt_gatt.h
+++ b/include/nuttx/wireless/bluetooth/bt_gatt.h
@@ -620,5 +620,13 @@ struct bt_gatt_discover_params_s
   uint16_t group_end_handle;
 
+  /* Terminal ATT status, valid during destroy.  Zero means success; a
+   * remote Attribute Not Found is reported as BT_ATT_ERR_ATTRIBUTE_NOT_FOUND.
+   * Malformed responses use BT_ATT_ERR_INVALID_PDU and failed pagination
+   * uses BT_ATT_ERR_UNLIKELY.
+   */
+
+  uint8_t result;
+
   /* Private data */
 
   FAR void *p_data;
diff --git a/wireless/bluetooth/bt_gatt.c b/wireless/bluetooth/bt_gatt.c
--- a/wireless/bluetooth/bt_gatt.c
+++ b/wireless/bluetooth/bt_gatt.c
